{
  "_readme": [
    "Stratum/DATUM endpoint list for pool-probe.py.",
    "'label' MUST match the attribution label reorg-watch.py prints, that is the join key.",
    "Fill in host/port for each endpoint a pool advertises publicly. One entry per",
    "advertised endpoint; a pool offering both v1 and DATUM gets two entries.",
    "'expect' is what you think it is (stratum-v1 | datum | unknown); the probe records",
    "what it actually finds and does not trust this field.",
    "'source' is where you got it (pool website, miner config, Discord, date). Keep it,",
    "it is the difference between evidence and hearsay.",
    "Leave an endpoint with host:'' and the probe skips it.",
    "'terms' is what the pool's own site says: sv1_fee, datum_fee, payout, with 'source' and 'checked' date. Self-reported; the survey passes it through unverified.",
    "'sv1_closed' records a pool's own statement that its stratum path is closed, with the date and page; the probe still tests the ports.",
    "'changes' is a short dated list of what pools changed, taken from their own pages; the page shows it newest first next to what the chain shows.",
    "'closed': true on an endpoint marks one the pool's own site says is closed; it is still probed, but the page does not offer it.",
    "'unclaimed': true on an endpoint means a third party named it, not the pool; it is probed and shown but never counted as the pool's own claim."
  ],
